gm-method (spoint 2026-07-01 editor Add menu + TickHandler relevanceRadius bug detail): TickHandler.js's relevanceRadius>0 snapshot path silently dropped ALL entity-removal notifications to already-connected clients via an empty-array-truthiness short-circuit -- a shared always-empty _precomputedRemoved array was handed into encodeDeltaFromCache for every existing player, so the array being present (but empty) short-circuited the real per-player removal fallback before it could compute anything. A deleted entity vanished from the scene hierarchy on the editor side but its client mesh/collider never got torn down for any world with relevanceRadius set. Fix: always pass undefined instead of the shared empty array, letting each player's own prevMap fallback compute its real removal set. General lesson: a "cache co-located with a per-call computation" pattern is dangerous when the cache can be validly empty AND used as a JS truthy/falsy gate -- an empty array is truthy, so `cachedRemoved || computeRemoved()` silently prefers the empty cache forever once one exists, never falling through to the real computation.